claimed: intent-temporal-slots — a When slot takes ISO-8601 and refuses everything else through SIso, so "next thursday" and "jeudi prochain" cannot be filled and the model does the conversion with the schema merely checking it. Build the Duckling-equivalent over okay-lex/okay-parse: a total parser from an English temporal phrase to a resolved date, relative to a supplied "now" so it is deterministic and testable in the DEFAULT gate with no model at all -- which is the point, since every other lane in this line has cost a live run. Scope stated up front and kept: English, the phrase shapes that actually appear in scheduling mail (weekday names, next/this/last, tomorrow, in N days, explicit dates, times of day), and a REFUSAL rather than a guess for anything else -- a temporal parser that guesses is worse than one that declines, because a wrong date is acted on and a declined one is asked about.
